    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37913" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπακμ-άζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be in one's prime,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.33
			</span></i>; also of things, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				2.434
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aristaenet.
				2.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hld.
				7.8
			</span></i>: metaph., <i>come to its height,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Abd.</u>
				17
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				1.18e
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπήκμασαν οἱ ἐτησίαι</span>”
				<i>were blowing hard,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					15.1.17
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> of persons,
				<i>flourish in succession to,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					<u>Pomp.</u>
					4
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἐπακμάσαντες</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>; also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νέα ἐ. παλαιοῖς,</span> of
			animals and crops, <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				1.28
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				2.424
			</span></i>.</div>
